From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:55:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 050/371] teleport: a pirate can teleport to a friend on land,
 and lands beside him

Teleporting to a friend asked the server for the main world by an empty
name. No world has that name, so the server stopped with "Cannot
initiate teleport for unknown world" and the pirate stayed where he was,
his teleport lock still set until he logged out.

Three more things were wrong on the way:
- A friend or crewmate the client can't see was asked through a handle
  that never reaches him, so nothing happened at all.
- A refusal from the server never reached the pirate, so a friend in
  jail, in a teleport or on the same island also left him locked.
- Had it worked, he would have landed at the island's spawn point, not
  by his friend.

- The server's teleportToFriend checks the friend: in this district, on
  land in the main world (an island or a building), not in jail, not
  busy (his teleport flags, the same reasons his own client gives). It
  teleports the pirate into the friend's world and area, three feet in
  front of the friend, facing him (the island's spawn point when the
  server has no position for the friend).
- A refusal is sent back as the friend's own client would answer, with
  the reason; the client shows the game's own message ("Sorry, X is in
  jail.") and lets go of its teleport lock. A friend on the same island
  answers "X is already here!" (new string NoTeleportToSameArea).
- A friend on a ship is refused ("Sorry, X's ship is full at the
  moment."): the old way onto a friend's ship left the pirate at his own
  last spawn point, still locked.
- The client asks the server directly for a friend it can't see; a
  friend it can see is still asked through his own client first.

The teleport to a ship by the ship's own id (requestTeleportToShip) is
unchanged.

AI and client: needs a server restart and the two client files
(pirates/instance/DistributedTeleportMgr.py,
pirates/piratesbase/PLocalizerEnglish.py). An old client still teleports
to a friend it can see, but not to one it can't, and after a refusal it
stays locked as before.

